From b24262e2cee8a0335847bb15ec8a9d6bc6846587 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:25:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: validate the encoder frame size in try_fmt

iris_venc_try_fmt() only corrected an unsupported pixel format; any
width and height were accepted by TRY_FMT and S_FMT, for the raw queue
and for the bitstream queue alike. The checks that exist later look at
the raw size only (iris_check_resolution_supported() uses fmt_src), and
never at the size the encoder is asked to produce, so:

 - a size outside the 128..8192 range the driver itself advertises was
   accepted without adjustment, with the failure only showing up when
   streaming starts;
 - the bitstream queue could be set larger than the raw frame, which is
   an upscale. The VPU scaler only scales down; the firmware even has a
   dedicated error code for it (HFI_ERR_SESSION_UPSCALE_NOT_SUPPORTED),
   which the Gen1 response handler only reports at debug level, so
   the failure is close to invisible.

Clamp both queues to the platform limits, and clamp the bitstream size
to the raw size so the only encoder-side resize the driver can request
is a downscale. V4L2 expects the driver to adjust the format rather than
accept an invalid one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XHbRyvZ53xawh6pBdmacMe
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c
index f60adff2f..a1acdc8b9 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c
@@ -178,6 +178,7 @@ int iris_venc_enum_fmt(struct iris_inst *inst, struct v4l2_fmtdesc *f)
 
 int iris_venc_try_fmt(struct iris_inst *inst, struct v4l2_format *f)
 {
+	struct platform_inst_caps *caps = inst->core->iris_platform_data->inst_caps;
 	struct v4l2_pix_format_mplane *pixmp = &f->fmt.pix_mp;
 	struct v4l2_format *f_inst;
 	bool supported;
@@ -210,6 +211,22 @@ int iris_venc_try_fmt(struct iris_inst *inst, struct v4l2_format *f)
 
 	pixmp->num_planes = 1;
 
+	/* Stay inside what the hardware can encode instead of accepting any size */
+	pixmp->width = clamp(pixmp->width, caps->min_frame_width, caps->max_frame_width);
+	pixmp->height = clamp(pixmp->height, caps->min_frame_height, caps->max_frame_height);
+
+	/*
+	 * The VPU scaler can only scale down: the firmware rejects an upscale
+	 * (HFI_ERR_SESSION_UPSCALE_NOT_SUPPORTED), so never let the encoded size
+	 * grow beyond the raw frame.
+	 */
+	if (f->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE) {
+		pixmp->width = min(pixmp->width,
+				   max(inst->enc_raw_width, caps->min_frame_width));
+		pixmp->height = min(pixmp->height,
+				    max(inst->enc_raw_height, caps->min_frame_height));
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
